(4002877, 571315, 70181, '<td valign="top">Unfortunately, the ground is too dark and you can''t see the combine very well.  This would have turned out better in advanced editing where you could brighten the ground without blowing out the sky.  Not much you can do in basic editing.  But it''s a good composition with an interesting subject.</td>', 'Unfortunately, the ground is too dark and you can''t see the combine very well.  This would have turned out better in advanced editing where you could brighten the ground without blowing out the sky.  Not much you can do in basic editing.  But it''s a good composition with an interesting subject.', '2007-08-16 00:27:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(4002882, 569859, 70181, '<td valign="top">Nice composition.  I like the lines.  And I love that sky.</td>', 'Nice composition.  I like the lines.  And I love that sky.', '2007-08-16 00:29:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(4002885, 569859, 3102, '<td valign="top">This shot turns out to be my 150,000th vote on DPChallenge... so to commemorate the milestone, I''m going to offer a much more thorough critique than I would normally ever take the time to give (um... lucky you...!?).<br/> <br/>Actually, I''m very glad this is the milestone shot, because I like it a lot.  Just two votes ago, I was casting my vote for an obvious attempt at a brown ribbon, so I''m quite thankful to be at this shot!<br/> <br/>Anyway... on to the meat.  Lots of farming shots in the challenge, naturally.  I like the composition here.  Keeping the tractor off-center helps make the shot more interesting, and the lines of the crops give it a great sense of rhythm.  The colors feel a little muted to me, as if the green could have been a little more green, but even as it is, the colors of the crops blend nicely with the sky.<br/> <br/>As a bit of a nitpick, I probably would have liked it a little better without the fence in the foreground.  I kinda doubt the farmer would have appreciated you knocking it down, though :)<br/> <br/>I wouldn''t be surprised if someone posted a note suggesting that the shot should be rotated to provide a level horizon, but I would think it''s fine as is.  After all, it is apparently on a hill.<br/> <br/>Can''t think of too much more to add.  Again, lots of farming shots in the challenge, so it''s a little hard to really stand out above all of them, but this is definitely among the better ones I''ve seen.  I''m giving it a 7.</td>', 'This shot turns out to be my 150,000th vote on DPChallenge... so to commemorate the milestone, I''m going to offer a much more thorough critique than I would normally ever take the time to give (um... lucky you...!?). Actually, I''m very glad this is the milestone shot, because I like it a lot.  Just two votes ago, I was casting my vote for an obvious attempt at a brown ribbon, so I''m quite thankful to be at this shot! Anyway... on to the meat.  Lots of farming shots in the challenge, naturally.  I like the composition here.  Keeping the tractor off-center helps make the shot more interesting, and the lines of the crops give it a great sense of rhythm.  The colors feel a little muted to me, as if the green could have been a little more green, but even as it is, the colors of the crops blend nicely with the sky. As a bit of a nitpick, I probably would have liked it a little better without the fence in the foreground.  I kinda doubt the farmer would have appreciated you knocking it down, though :) I wouldn''t be surprised if someone posted a note suggesting that the shot should be rotated to provide a level horizon, but I would think it''s fine as is.  After all, it is apparently on a hill. Can''t think of too much more to add.  Again, lots of farming shots in the challenge, so it''s a little hard to really stand out above all of them, but this is definitely among the better ones I''ve seen.  I''m giving it a 7.', '2007-08-16 00:30:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(4002887, 571874, 70181, '<td valign="top">Good use of a foreground element.  Nice infrared shot.</td>', 'Good use of a foreground element.  Nice infrared shot.', '2007-08-16 00:31:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(4002894, 570236, 70181, '<td valign="top">Clean and simple.  The color looks a little overdone, but overall, I like the shot.</td>', 'Clean and simple.  The color looks a little overdone, but overall, I like the shot.', '2007-08-16 00:33:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(4002904, 569876, 82294, '<td valign="top">this photo deserves zero...I''m tired of seeing it..its in every event..it should be band from the competition</td>', 'this photo deserves zero...I''m tired of seeing it..its in every event..it should be band from the competition', '2007-08-16 00:37:20.000000', NULL, 1),
