(4034483, 569165, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>What an interesting shot!  I like the colors, they don''t overwhelm you and add just a touch of life to the shot, as well as the wind blowing the flags around.  Very nice.<br/> <br/>I''m not so sure about the crop though.  Lots of things calling for my attention, the pole on the right, the tree on the left..... Taking out my magic envelopes and taking both of those elements out of the shot made a huge difference in the lines and the flow of the overall picture.  It really helped me focus on the flags and the lines.<br/> <br/>Overall a great effort and as for as being a rural landscape, things in the air are just as much a part of our landscape and world as the things on the ground and the horizon.  Well done and good luck in future challenges.<br/> <br/>Deannda</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! What an interesting shot!  I like the colors, they don''t overwhelm you and add just a touch of life to the shot, as well as the wind blowing the flags around.  Very nice. I''m not so sure about the crop though.  Lots of things calling for my attention, the pole on the right, the tree on the left..... Taking out my magic envelopes and taking both of those elements out of the shot made a huge difference in the lines and the flow of the overall picture.  It really helped me focus on the flags and the lines. Overall a great effort and as for as being a rural landscape, things in the air are just as much a part of our landscape and world as the things on the ground and the horizon.  Well done and good luck in future challenges. Deannda', '2007-08-28 00:21:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4034924, 571835, 67152, '<td valign="top">Hi Junie - i was looking through the photos in this challenge and noticed this was your photo.  I had meant to leave this one a comment during voting, but I guess it didn''t stick...so here it goes<br/> <br/>I can see what was so interesting to you about this location - the nice warm lighting, the beautiful horse, the intense greens and blues of the grass and hills.  The image itself didn''t quite come together as I think it could have.  Here a couple of things I noticed:<br/> <br/>1. the positioning of a centered horizon often creates a static feel - placing less of the mostly uninteresting sky in the image would have brought more detail and life to the shot<br/>2. the fence line in front is actually pretty interesting - a lower angle on this shot to bring more of the fence in view would have added some nice textures (everyone likes a barbed wire fence!)<br/>3. even with all the sky and grass - it seems a little ''closed'' - taking the photo down and moving back a bit to bring more fence and more of the foreground in view would likely help add those textures and reduce the bright sky<br/>4. the sky seems a bit bright and seems to overwhelm the photo a bit - taking down the levels on the brights (or having less sky in view) would help here<br/> <br/>It is a great spot and you did a nice job of capturing the warmth of the day.  I think a few small adjustments would have let us see that beautiful story that you saw when you took this photo.<br/> <br/>Peter<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-08-28 06:49:24.</i></td>', 'Hi Junie - i was looking through the photos in this challenge and noticed this was your photo.  I had meant to leave this one a comment during voting, but I guess it didn''t stick...so here it goes I can see what was so interesting to you about this location - the nice warm lighting, the beautiful horse, the intense greens and blues of the grass and hills.  The image itself didn''t quite come together as I think it could have.  Here a couple of things I noticed: 1. the positioning of a centered horizon often creates a static feel - placing less of the mostly uninteresting sky in the image would have brought more detail and life to the shot2. the fence line in front is actually pretty interesting - a lower angle on this shot to bring more of the fence in view would have added some nice textures (everyone likes a barbed wire fence!)3. even with all the sky and grass - it seems a little ''closed'' - taking the photo down and moving back a bit to bring more fence and more of the foreground in view would likely help add those textures and reduce the bright sky4. the sky seems a bit bright and seems to overwhelm the photo a bit - taking down the levels on the brights (or having less sky in view) would help here It is a great spot and you did a nice job of capturing the warmth of the day.  I think a few small adjustments would have let us see that beautiful story that you saw when you took this photo. Peter', '2007-08-28 07:47:24.000000', '2007-08-28 07:49:24.000000', 0),
